How the extension is loaded (critical context)
The extension does not inject anything itself. It relies on the Custom CSS and JS Loader extension (be5invis.vscode-custom-css) to patch workbench.html with our script. This means:
Settings changes require a Custom CSS reload cycle: Disable Custom CSS and JS → Enable Custom CSS and JS → Reload Window.
Caching is aggressive. When the user says "new version isn't loading", that's almost always Custom CSS cache. Tell them to run the cycle above.
rtl-config.js exists because settings from package.json (rtlForVsCodeAgents.*) need to reach the injected script — we write a tiny JS file that sets window.__RTL_CONFIG__ and is loaded before the main script.
Cursor-specific selectors already handled (do not rediscover)
Agent message bubbles: .markdown-root > div (in CONFIG.chatSelectors).
User input box: .composer-input div[contenteditable="true"] (in CONFIG.inputSelectors).
User message bubbles: .composer-human-message-content and .composer-questionnaire-toolbar — handled dynamically by processCursorUserMessages() which applies both direction: rtl and text-align: right only when Hebrew/Arabic is detected.
Code blocks (must stay LTR even with Hebrew comments): .composer-message-codeblock, .ui-default-code, .ui-code-block-default-code — forced LTR in ensureCodeBlocksLTR().
Streamdown streaming spans: [data-sd-animate="true"], [data-streamdown] — set to unicode-bidi: normal !important to avoid word reversal in bold/italic during streaming.
Monaco editor bleed prevention: view-line elements inside .monaco-mouse-cursor-text are skipped when monacoRtlEnabled === false (the default).
Workflow for any new fix
Reproduce / understand. Ask the user for: which Cursor UI surface (agent message? user message? input? code block? streaming?), Hebrew or English, screenshot if possible, and the relevant DOM classes from DevTools.
Edit rtl-for-vs-code-agents.js (or src/extension.js if it's a settings/wiring issue). Prefer:
Adding/extending an existing selector list over creating a new function.
Conditional JS (check text content) over broad !important CSS, when the same selector can legitimately hold either LTR or RTL content.
unicode-bidi: normal on inner spans when streamdown causes word reversal.
Bump package.json version. Patch bump for fixes (e.g. 1.0.x → 1.0.y). Minor bump for new features.
